s lanes not exercised (`ENTITY_POSTGRES_URL` unset). Full log: `home-path:sha256:641252b4ce35d5e337c686d5e6d709a6b0504d5ca64c4dc4b3fc8822adfd1f57`.\n\n## 4. Findings (commit 11cc13e10, worktree above)\n\n**1 — `findings` on a migrated plan compares the rounds by id, while the unit says the order now comes from the authority.**\n\n* **file:line** `crates/edge/aep-cli/src/planning.rs:5536` (`reviews_of`: `.journal()` is `None` on `Plan::Eventlog`, `.unwrap_or_default()` at :5545 leaves `order` empty, and the sort key falls to `frontmatter.id`).\n* **what was measured** `store_writer_control.rs:2297`, exit 101: two rounds on a migrated plan, `zulu` recorded before the cut-over and `alpha` after it, and the default pair is `from: review-result:alpha, to: review-result:zulu` — the second round read as the earlier one, which is the ledger the fix's own comment (:5524-5530) describes as calling every resolved finding new. The store does know the order: `history review-result:zulu` gives `created` at `…21:21:06Z`, `alpha` at `…21:21:10Z`, both from `entries_from_the_contract`.\n* **what reaches it** `aep plan artifact findings <id>` without `--from/--to` on any migrated plan whose review ids do not sort in recording order — reviewer-named rounds (`alpha`/`zulu`), or numbered ones past nine (`round-10` sorts before `round-9`). The unit's own case (:1782) names its rounds `alpha`/`beta`, where id order and recording order agree, so it cannot tell the two apart. Contract item 5 (“orders stably”) holds; the CHANGELOG (`CHANGELOG.md:26-28`: “the order `plan artifact findings` compares two rounds in … now come from the authority rather than from the legacy `journal.jsonl`”) and `website/docs/reference/cli.md:99` (“the two most recent `review-result` records”) do not.\n* **base** by reading `git show af2af7e74:…/planning.rs` :5493-5517: `order` came from the frozen journal, so `zulu` had `Some(k)` and `alpha` `None`, and `None < Some` puts `alpha` first — the same wrong pair. The misorder is older than this diff; the claim to have fixed it is this diff's, which is why the origin is `introduced` and the route is back to the implementor.\n* **verdict** NEEDS-CHANGE · **origin** introduced · **severity** warning\n* **named correction (not applied)** on an Eventlog plan take the order from the `Created` entry's `at` in `Opened::history_entries` (id as the tie-break for the same-second case the doc comment worries about) — or, if id order is the accepted answer, say so in `CHANGELOG.md:26-28`, `cli.md:99` and the `findings` doc, and drop “from the authority” for this verb.\n\n**2 — every `validate` on an Eventlog plan now makes one contract read per artifact.**\n\n* **file:line** `crates/edge/aep-cli/src/planning.rs:892` (`history_entries`: `self.report.documents.keys()` × `entries_from_the_contract`), reached from `validate` at `:6033`, which calls `reviews_without_an_outcome` on **every** run — `--strict` decides only the exit code.\n* **what was measured** on the 3-artifact fixture case 2a left behind (`…/tmp/aep-public-writer-control-1644783-0`), three runs each, wall clock: `validate --strict --outcome-within 7` 7325/7310/7346 ms; plain `validate` 7278/7275/7347 ms; `review-value` 6534/6538/6553 ms; `explain story:one` (exactly one contract read) 6160/6145/6030 ms; `list` (no history read) 5005/4963/4924 ms. So ≈5.0 s to open the plan plus ≈0.8–1.1 s per artifact history read, linear in N. At base the same function returned early on Eventlog with zero reads (that was finding 1 of the base review); this diff introduces the N reads.\n* **what reaches it** gate step 3 `task plan-check` (`Taskfile.yml:124-133`, described at :128 as “Local, clock-free and sub-second”) runs `validate` without `--strict`; `aep doctor` reuses the same accumulation. The repository's own store — this wave's migration target — holds 299 planning documents today (`find …/.engineering/planning -name '*.md' | wc -l`); at the measured slope a `validate` on it after migration is a projected 4–5 minutes. Projected, not measured at that size: the 12-artifact probe fixture the first attempt was building is still being written by its orphan loop (§6) and was not free for an unloaded run.\n* **verdict** CONFIRMED (mechanism and slope measured; the 299-artifact figure is a projection) · **origin** introduced · **severity** warning\n* **named correction (not applied)** bound the reads to the artifacts the class needs — the `review-result` documents (for `Created`) and the artifacts they `reviews` (for the `review_outcome` records, which are recorded against the reviewed artifact) — and skip the class entirely when the plan holds no `review-result`; `review_records`/`outcomes_of` need only the reviews and their targets likewise. A store-wide history read on the authority, if the backend can offer one, is the larger fix.\n\n## 5. Reviewed and not faulted\n\n* Contract 1 — `grep -n \"self\\.files\\|opened\\.files\" planning.rs`: the only remaining reads are `Opened::missing` (:819) and `Opened::path_of` (:827), both answering where a document is; the five history readers go through `journal()` or `history_entries()`.\n* Contract 2 — the unit's gated-move case, plus :2097 (a pre-migration record is counted once, not twice through retained-line-plus-event) and :2154 (a retried `--command-identity` is one record).\n* Contract 3 — the unit's post-migration case, plus :2321 for the pre-migration `review_outcome`: once, not zero, not twice, across `show`, `review-value` and `validate`.\n* Contract 4 — the adopted case is green here; the `Created` instant of a migrated artifact is the retained line's original `at` (`history story:one` on the fixture is exactly one `created` at `2026-01-01T00:00:00Z`; no import event surfaces as an entry), so `--outcome-within` ages are right, and an artifact with no retained line has no `Created` and is left out exactly as on a Markdown plan.\n* Contract 6 — `tests/drift.rs`, `tests/planning_cli.rs`, `tests/wave_derivation.rs` byte-identical to base and green (6/86/13); SQLite and Postgres hit the `!matches!(self.plan, Plan::Eventlog …)` early return at :896 and answer empty, by reading.\n* Contract 7 — no hunk of the diff touches the `asserted` provenance list (:6104-6140), `verify` or `inspect`.\n* Hybrid (brief item 4) — `HybridBackend<R>` is `EntityBackend<Composite<R>, MarkdownProjection>` (`aep-backend-hybrid/src/lib.rs:294`), so the root `journal.jsonl` is written by the plan's own projection on every command whatever the policy; it does not freeze the way a migrated Eventlog's does, and `journal()` returning the root store is the right record.\n* `history_entries`'s `.ok()` — `resolve` cannot fail for an id the backend itself listed, and `entries_of` fails only on an authority `plan store verify` already reports (duplicated ordinal, disagreeing source); no documented workflow reaches a silent omission, so not filed.\n* The foreign-document case (:1834) carries no `#[ignore]`, and each of its three assertion messages names `story:unowned-document-in-eventlog-projection-is-reported` and says to rewrite the assertion as the refusal — never to loosen.\n* Formatting and lints green after my additions.\n\n## 6. Paths written outside the worktree\n\nAll under the assigned scratch parent except the last:\n\n1. `home-path:sha256:192b67b419c5a1a3c4a9ffe1dc9f2fc97e67d2dc61fb6468d2cbd08cc9be77d5` — the assigned `TMPDIR` (created by me). Holds `aep-writer-control-*` socket directories (8), the fixture case 2a left behind (`aep-public-writer-control-1644783-0`, 3 artifacts, used for §4.2's timings and kept for the second pass), and `aep-public-writer-control-1298446-0` — the first attempt's cost-probe fixture, **still being written** by the orphan loop below.\n2. `home-path:sha256:58a8ff50b839f573e27eba35b02528088fb096defb149cfe1fd1b3e86066ae66`, `alone-<case>.log` ×4, `clippy.log`, `clippy2.log`, `fmt.log`, `fmt2.log`, `suite.log` — one level above the assigned `tmp/`, which is a small deviation from the triple and is named here.\n3. This report, at the path the brief names.\n\nNothing under `/tmp`. No planning-store write, no `aep plan artifact` write verb, no git write command, no worktree command other than the lease hooks for session `ess-u2r1-fable-20260920` (start, four heartbeats, end).\n\n**Orphan from the killed first attempt (for the coordinator).** `zsh` PID 1311658 (started 23:00:01, cwd the probe fixture) is running `for n in 01..12; aep plan artifact new story probe-$n …; done` followed by timed `validate` runs, using this worktree's `target/debug/aep`; its stdout died with its session. At 23:33 it was on `probe-11`. I did not kill it: it is disposable and its fixture is the 13-artifact plan the second pass can time. Each of its `new story` writes takes 2–5 minutes (file mtimes 23:00→23:19 for eight, `probe-09` 23:19:29→~23:25), an order of magnitude slower than the same verb inside the lane's cases; I found no wait constant explaining it and did not measure further — an observation, not a finding on this diff.\n\n```findings\n- file: crates/edge/aep-cli/src/planning.rs\n  line: 5536\n  category: contract-drift\n  severity: warning\n  verdict: NEEDS-CHANGE\n  origin: introduced\n  message: on an Eventlog plan reviews_of takes no order from any record and falls to the id, so `findings` compares two rounds whose ids sort against their recording order the wrong way round (from alpha, to zulu, measured at store_writer_control.rs:2297), while CHANGELOG.md:26-28 says the order now comes from the authority and website/docs/reference/cli.md:99 promises the two most recent reviews; the misorder predates the diff, the claim to have fixed it is the diff's.\n- file: crates/edge/aep-cli/src/planning.rs\n  line: 892\n  category: judgement\n  severity: warning\n  verdict: CONFIRMED\n  origin: introduced\n  message: history_entries makes one contract read per artifact and validate (planning.rs:6033) computes reviews_without_an_outcome on every run whether or not --strict, so a migrated plan's validate costs about 5.0 s plus 0.8-1.1 s per artifact (0 reads 5.0 s, 1 read 6.1 s, 3 reads 7.3 s, measured), against Taskfile.yml:128's sub-second plan-check and a projected 4-5 minutes for the 299-document store this wave migrates.\n```\n","document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"ent-52c9af3702baa4ebd3ce995265b96446","locator":"ep://planning/store/review-result/evidence-on-hand-review-1","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":1,"type":"aep.review-result/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"unit: task:evidence-on-hand-v2-journal — commit 11cc13e10074eb409e213f2c91e1d1f95cd5231a (base af2af7e74), worktree home-path:sha256:ab2661d0520012b3da0a3a044d25bcbfe52de26bc0055f931dacb2fef4d1e30a detached at that commit plus 403 test-only lines\nverdict: red\ncases: executed 587→591, red 1\norigin: introduced 2, pre-existing 0, undecided 0\nwrote-outside-worktree: home-path:sha256:78816392475889d9a4b1112901e396d5fcc4cdc1ea7b4e7f303edbd3e7a8a47f,build.log,alone-*.log (4),clippy.log,clippy2.log,fmt.log,fmt2.log,suite.log} and this report (§6)\nneeds-coordinator: yes — a cost-probe shell loop from the killed first attempt (zsh 1311658, started 23:00:01) is still alive and writing `probe-NN` stories into a fixture under the assigned scratch directory; stop it or let it finish (§6)\n\n## 1. `git --no-pager diff --stat`\n\n```\n crates/edge/aep-cli/tests/store_writer_control.rs | 403 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 403 insertions(+)\n```\n\nOne path, a test file. No implementation file was edited, not even briefly; no probe needed a scratch copy of one. No untracked files in the tree (no `aep … --store` was run with the worktree as cwd, so no `.engineering/*.lock` files were left).\n\n## 2. Cases — `crates/edge/aep-cli/tests/store_writer_control.rs`\n\nLines 2051–2319 were written by the killed first attempt and are kept as input; I changed one helper s