thority rather than from the legacy `journal.jsonl`”) and `website/docs/reference/cli.md:99` (“the two most recent `review-result` records”) do not.\n* **base** by reading `git show af2af7e74:…/planning.rs` :5493-5517: `order` came from the frozen journal, so `zulu` had `Some(k)` and `alpha` `None`, and `None < Some` puts `alpha` first — the same wrong pair. The misorder is older than this diff; the claim to have fixed it is this diff's, which is why the origin is `introduced` and the route is back to the implementor.\n* **verdict** NEEDS-CHANGE · **origin** introduced · **severity** warning\n* **named correction (not applied)** on an Eventlog plan take the order from the `Created` entry's `at` in `Opened::history_entries` (id as the tie-break for the same-second case the doc comment worries about) — or, if id order is the accepted answer, say so in `CHANGELOG.md:26-28`, `cli.md:99` and the `findings` doc, and drop “from the authority” for this verb.\n\n**2 — every `validate` on an Eventlog plan now makes one contract read per artifact.**\n\n* **file:line** `crates/edge/aep-cli/src/planning.rs:892` (`history_entries`: `self.report.documents.keys()` × `entries_from_the_contract`), reached from `validate` at `:6033`, which calls `reviews_without_an_outcome` on **every** run — `--strict` decides only the exit code.\n* **what was measured** on the 3-artifact fixture case 2a left behind (`…/tmp/aep-public-writer-control-1644783-0`), three runs each, wall clock: `validate --strict --outcome-within 7` 7325/7310/7346 ms; plain `validate` 7278/7275/7347 ms; `review-value` 6534/6538/6553 ms; `explain story:one` (exactly one contract read) 6160/6145/6030 ms; `list` (no history read) 5005/4963/4924 ms. So ≈5.0 s to open the plan plus ≈0.8–1.1 s per artifact history read, linear in N. At base the same function returned early on Eventlog with zero reads (that was finding 1 of the base review); this diff introduces the N reads.\n* **what reaches it** gate step 3 `task plan-check` (`Taskfile.yml:124-133`, described at :128 as “Local, clock-free and sub-second”) runs `validate` without `--strict`; `aep doctor` reuses the same accumulation. The repository's own store — this wave's migration target — holds 299 planning documents today (`find …/.engineering/planning -name '*.md' | wc -l`); at the measured slope a `validate` on it after migration is a projected 4–5 minutes. Projected, not measured at that size: the 12-artifact probe fixture the first attempt was building is still being written by its orphan loop (§6) and was not free for an unloaded run.\n* **verdict** CONFIRMED (mechanism and slope measured; the 299-artifact figure is a projection) · **origin** introduced · **severity** warning\n* **named correction (not applied)** bound the reads to the artifacts the class needs — the `review-result` documents (for `Created`) and the artifacts they `reviews` (for the `review_outcome` records, which are recorded against the reviewed artifact) — and skip the class entirely when the plan holds no `review-result`; `review_records`/`outcomes_of` need only the reviews and their targets likewise. A store-wide history read on the authority, if the backend can offer one, is the larger fix.\n\n## 5. Reviewed and not faulted\n\n* Contract 1 — `grep -n \"self\\.files\\|opened\\.files\" planning.rs`: the only remaining reads are `Opened::missing` (:819) and `Opened::path_of` (:827), both answering where a document is; the five history readers go through `journal()` or `history_entries()`.\n* Contract 2 — the unit's gated-move case, plus :2097 (a pre-migration record is counted once, not twice through retained-line-plus-event) and :2154 (a retried `--command-identity` is one record).\n* Contract 3 — the unit's post-migration case, plus :2321 for the pre-migration `review_outcome`: once, not zero, not twice, across `show`, `review-value` and `validate`.\n* Contract 4 — the adopted case is green here; the `Created` instant of a migrated artifact is the retained